From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 19:32:08 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7615: fix NULL deref in mt7615_mac_set_rates

mt7615_add_interface() never initializes the vif backpointer of the
per-vif embedded sta, unlike mt7915 and mt7996. When a rate control
probe frame goes out on the BSS wcid (mac80211 hands frames over
without a station once the station is no longer uploaded, e.g. during
teardown), mt7615_mac_set_rates() dereferences the NULL sta->vif while
reading the omac index:

  Unable to handle kernel read from unreadable memory at virtual
  address 0000000000000002
  ...
  pc : mt7615_mac_set_rates
  lr : mt7615_tx_prepare_skb

Initialize the pointer as the other connac drivers do.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 mt7615/main.c |    1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/mt7615/main.c
+++ b/mt7615/main.c
@@ -225,6 +225,7 @@ static int mt7615_add_interface(struct i
 
 	INIT_LIST_HEAD(&mvif->sta.wcid.poll_list);
 	mvif->sta.wcid.idx = idx;
+	mvif->sta.vif = mvif;
 	mt76_wcid_init(&mvif->sta.wcid, mvif->mt76.band_idx);
 
 	mt7615_mac_wtbl_update(dev, idx,
